import Algebra.Group.Hom

/-! # Products of a family of groups

Mathlib: `Mathlib/Algebra/Notation/Pi/Defs.lean` (`Pi.mul_apply`, …),
`Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Pi/Basic.lean` (the group), `Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Pi/Hom.lean`
(`Pi.evalMonoidHom`, `MonoidHom.pi`).

`∀ i, f i` is a group, pointwise: `(x * y) i = x i * y i`. This generalizes `G × H` (a family
indexed by two points) to any index type, including infinite ones; `G^ι = ι → G` is the case
of a constant family.

`evalMonoidHom_apply` and `MonoidHom.pi_apply` are generated by `@[simps]` in Mathlib. -/

